#![enable(implicit_some)]
// FROZEN copy (see projectiles.ron) of assets/config/unit_defs.ron as it was when the projectiles
// scenario was pinned (WP5.2). A balance change of the shipped file does not move its checksum.
// Unit, structure and mission-object definitions (WP3.1): one record per role of
// content/units.md, with its design-target stats. Read by sf_data::units, which
// checks every reference; docs/rules/units.md describes each field.
//
// `kind` IS THE PERMANENT NUMBER of a role: the simulation's `Kind`, and what
// scenarios, saves and replays name it by. Pick the next free number for a new
// role; never change a number, and never reuse one. Records may stand in any
// order. To remove a role, delete its record and add a tombstone with its number
// to `retired_units` at the end of this file. Adding a role is only a new record
// here (and weapons in weapon_defs.ron, if it needs new ones): no Rust change.
//
// Units of measure: distances, sizes and sight in cells (1 cell = 4 m, B12);
// speed in cells per game second (20 ticks); build_seconds in game seconds;
// turn_rate in facing steps (256 per full turn) per tick; turret_rate (optional, vehicles with a
// glTF `turret` part) the same for the turret, which turns apart from the hull (WP4.5); cost in credits;
// power in power units (+ produces, - uses); hp abstract.
//
// What content/units.md states is used as is: roles, cost, power, hp, speed,
// weapon ranges, capacities and radii, and the faction that gets the role in
// its tech tree. Everything else is a placeholder, marked with a
// `placeholder:` comment on the record: build_seconds, turn_rate, size, sight,
// armor type, the footprints of mission structures and the model/icon choices
// (the testpack_v1 models stand in until real art, WP11.6; roles without a
// model use a primitive shape).
//
// Models (docs/rules/units.md): `model` is what a role is drawn with; the
// optional `models: { Meridian: Glb(..), Veyran: Glb(..) }` gives a faction
// its own look for the same role (a unit is drawn with its owner's entry, else
// with `model`, else with a primitive by category). Presentation only: the
// simulation never sees it. The infantry of art set v3 (assets/set_v3) is wired
// this way; decor (trees, rocks, ore stages, wrecks) is not a unit role and is
// not listed here.
//
// Strategic icons (WP3.6): `strategic_icon` is the base shape of the role's
// category (Square structures, Circle infantry, Triangle vehicles, HalfCircle
// vessels) and what it is drawn as without an `icon`; `icon` names the picture
// in assets/icons (docs/rules/icons.md). The bridge, the rail spur, the
// evidence crate and the ore field have no icon of their own: the base shape.
